<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lucius Postumius Albinus (consul 234 BC)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 216 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lucius Postumius Albinus was a Roman general, consul in 234 and 229 BCE. In 216 BCE, after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-cannae">Cannae</a>, he was sent against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gauls">Gauls</a> of the Po valley, but the Boii ambushed and destroyed his army in the Litana forest. He was killed while consul-elect for 215 BCE, and the Boii are said to have made his skull into a gilded cup.</p></div>
